{#
  The environment file every container unit of the service reads.

  `<AS>_HOST` is the provider's own service name and `<AS>_PORT` is the
  publication the mutator allocated for the edge. There is no name map and no
  `/etc/hosts`: the host name resolves because the unit carries
  `AddHost=<provider>:<alias>`.

  For a multi-database edge the variables are named `<AS>_<DB>_HOST`,
  `<AS>_<DB>_PORT` and `<AS>_<DB>_USER`, one set per database. The password
  is not written here; it arrives as a Secret named `<AS>_PASSWORD`.
#}
# Rendered by loom. Do not edit: the next render overwrites this file.
{% for variable, host, port, user in rows %}
{{ variable }}_HOST={{ host }}
{{ variable }}_PORT={{ port }}
{% if user %}{{ variable }}_USER={{ user }}
{% endif %}{% endfor %}
